[Music]  bookstores are portals to amazing  adventures and stories um brought right  to your fingertips literally i'm  self-educated i taught myself from books  by going to bookstores and so i'm so  passionate about reading because it can  change your life it teaches about  history geography humanity poetry love  just everything everything can be found  through reading but not everyone has  access  i was lucky when i was younger to be  able to go and purchase books or go to  the libraries and in manhattan there are  70 bookstores  to find your next great read  but head to the bronx and there's only  one  our next guest is a drew gooder  determined to change that one book at a  time please watch this  my name is latonya lavonne and i am from  the bronx i am the proud owner of bronx  bound books a bookstore on wheels right  now the bronx only has one brick and  mortar bookstore i believe a bookstore  should be a staple in every community  sometimes the kids in the bronx don't  have access to books until they are in  the school building my mission is to  make book ownership accessible and  affordable i purchased an old bus and  took out all the seats and flooring and  converted it into a beautiful bookstore  on wheels  we sell books at weekly farmer's markets  we visit schools  we go to shelters and we also host  various book drives there's such a huge  misconception about the people in the  bronx not wanting to read  i see young people all the time get  excited about reading  some kids come on and they can't believe  there's so many books others come on and  just sit down and just want to read they  think it's a genius idea for a bus to be  turned into a bookstore bronx phone  books feels like more than a dream come  true it's more than i could have ever  imagined it to be i wake up every day  thinking of new ways to improve how to  serve my community  and to make my dream even bigger  please  [Applause]  where did you forget this idea  i always wanted to own a bookstore  uh all my friends knew and i was just  having a conversation i was getting  ready to quit one of my jobs and my  friend vanessa said you know latonya you  have to just do the bookstore you keep  talking about this and i'm like well  the rents are so high in the bronx you  know gentrification is happening and  things are just really really changing  and i said i'm never going to be able to  afford a uh brick and mortar  so one day she just showed me a picture  of a book truck and that was all it took  for me to find the inspiration to do a  bookstore on wheels this is so genius  thank you  um  now this is personal for you will you  tell us why this is personal for you  well i grew up with my grandmother and  she was a teacher uh  not only did she teach the children in  the bronx  sometimes uh on any given saturday i  could come to my living room and i would  see her reading to her neighbors who  couldn't read so she would read lisa's  cable bills and just explained to them  why or when they needed to take their  medicine so seeing that showed me that  reading was just something that could  really change and save your life i see  the kids there  that's what you know  it does start there well we told the  publisher um  a kids company about all about you and  they're gonna give you five thousand  dollars worth of empowering educational  kids books wow  and then i'm gonna match it and give you  five thousand dollars just to enable  whatever you see fit and how to spend  that thank you so much  thank you so much i'm so in awe of what  you do and it is an honor to bring your  story to light to support you in our  tiny small way and just say keep going  because you are such a hero thank you  you are so amazing thank you latanya you  can learn more about bronx bound books  on the drewberrymore show.com where  you'll be featured on our website  [Music]  you

